      "content": "I see what you mean about balance, but it feels like you're saying the \"duty to actively work against prejudices\" is sort of the ultimate goal that everything else has to be measured against. If someone prioritizes traditional values or individual rights because they think those things are the fundamental building blocks of a stable society, are they actually contributing to a democracy, or are they just standing in the way of progress? Is there a way to be \"right\" in this debate, or is one side clearly more aligned with the future?",
